Falsifies `globally_unique_identifier_partition_table::verification::a_headers_fields_survive_the_round_trip`.

The defect: `encode_fields` writes `last_usable_lba` through a 32-bit truncation. Any disk past 2 TiB at 512-byte
blocks gets a header that decodes with a smaller usable range than it was built with.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(Header::decode_fields(&block), header)`.

diff --git a/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/header.rs b/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/header.rs
index 2495db796..ccb10a1c9 100644
--- a/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/header.rs
+++ b/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/header.rs
@@ -177,3 +177,3 @@ impl Header {
         put64(block, at::FIRST_USABLE_LBA, self.first_usable_lba);
-        put64(block, at::LAST_USABLE_LBA, self.last_usable_lba);
+        put64(block, at::LAST_USABLE_LBA, self.last_usable_lba as u32 as u64);
         block[at::DISK_GUID..at::DISK_GUID + 16].copy_from_slice(&guid::to_disk(self.disk_guid));
